* =============================================================================
* LM358  dual low-power operational amplifier  -  behavioural model (one half)
* =============================================================================
*
* WHAT THIS FILE IS
*   A simple ngspice macromodel of ONE amplifier of the LM358, built from the
*   typical values in the TI / onsemi LM358 datasheets. It is not the
*   manufacturer's model (TI's PSpice model could not be downloaded here),
*   but it covers what matters for a kHz audio-range filter:
*     - open-loop gain, gain-bandwidth product and slew rate
*     - single-supply operation: inputs and output work down to the
*       negative rail (GND), the output only reaches about Vcc - 1.5 V
*     - input bias current, input offset voltage, supply current
*   It does NOT model noise, crossover distortion, temperature drift or the
*   exact output current limits.
*
* DATASHEET VALUES USED (Vcc = 5 ... 30 V, Tamb = 25 C, typical)
*   open-loop gain       Avol = 100 V/mV (100 dB)
*   gain-bandwidth       GBW  = 0.7 MHz  (TI LM358; some sources give 1 MHz)
*   slew rate            SR   = 0.3 V/us
*   input offset         Vos  = 2 mV  (made a parameter, default 0)
*   input bias current   Ib   = 20 nA, flowing OUT of the inputs (PNP input stage)
*   output swing high    Voh  = Vcc - 1.5 V (light load)
*   output swing low     Vol  = about 5 mV above V- (light load)
*   input common mode    0 V ... Vcc - 1.5 V
*   supply current       Icc  = 0.7 mA for the whole package; half per amplifier
*
* HOW THE MODEL WORKS
*   1) Input stage: a transconductance G1 turns the differential input
*      voltage into a current, limited to +/- ISL. That limit is what sets
*      the slew rate.
*   2) That current charges the "compensation" capacitor C1 at node "int"
*      (the integrator inside every op-amp). R1 across C1 sets the DC gain:
*        DC gain = GM * R1 = 1e5 (100 dB)
*        unity-gain frequency = GM / (2*pi*C1) = 0.7 MHz
*        slew rate = ISL / C1 = 0.3 V/us
*   3) Diodes stop "int" from running away beyond the rails (so the model
*      recovers from overload quickly, like the real part).
*   4) Output stage: a voltage source copies "int", clipped to the range
*      V- + 5 mV ... V+ - 1.5 V, through 25 ohm output resistance.
*
* PINS:  inp  non-inverting input (+)
*        inn  inverting input (-)
*        vcc  positive supply
*        vee  negative supply (GND in a single-supply circuit)
*        out  output
* PARAMETER: vos = input offset voltage (default 0; try 2m or -2m to see
*            the effect of a typical offset)
*
* Use:  XU1 inp inn vcc 0 out LM358
* =============================================================================
.subckt LM358 inp inn vcc vee out vos=0
.param gm=88u c1=20p r1={1e5/gm} isl=6u
* ---- input stage ------------------------------------------------------------
* input bias currents, flowing out of the pins (PNP inputs), 20 nA each
IBP inp vee 20n
IBN inn vee 20n
* large differential and common-mode input resistance
RIN inp inn 10meg
* transconductance with a current limit: I = clamp(gm * (vin + vos), +/- isl)
* (current flows from vee into node int when the input is positive, so V(int) rises)
G1 vee int cur='max(min(gm*(v(inp)-v(inn)+vos), isl), -isl)'
* ---- integrator: sets DC gain, GBW and slew rate ----------------------------
C1 int vee {c1}
R1 int vee {r1}
* keep "int" between the rails (fast overload recovery)
* (EH copies the supply voltage so DH can clamp int to it; DL clamps to V-)
EH vh vee vcc vee 1
DH int vh DCL
DL vee int DCL
.model DCL D (IS=1e-14 N=0.2)
* ---- output stage: follows int, limited to the LM358's output range --------
* V- + 5 mV ... V+ - 1.5 V (the single-supply LM358 cannot reach V+)
BOUT oo vee V='max(min(v(int,vee), v(vcc,vee)-1.5), 0.005)'
ROUT oo out 25
* ---- supply current: 0.35 mA per amplifier (half of the package's 0.7 mA) ---
IQ vcc vee 0.35m
.ends LM358
